; effect4_engine — the OCaml host engine under the generated Lean machine
; (docs/research/2026-09-08-engine-brief.md; designs -a1-state, -a2-persistence,
; -a3-queue-query). Flat layout: every module is one `e4_*.ml` with its `.mli` and a
; property list at its head (ocaml/STANDARDS.md); tests live in test/ (their own dune).
; Dependencies: the stdlib, unix, threads, `effect4_eff` (the exact program wire, ocaml/eff —
; the generated engine opens Eff_types, the one program type), `effect4_clock` and `effect4_bytes` (bytes/: framing,
; hexadecimal, the 63-bit naturals, SHA-256) — nothing else without a measured need recorded
; in the design that asks for it. Builds as part of the estate workspace (ocaml/dune lists
; engine; `cd ocaml && dune build engine`).
(library
 (name effect4_engine)
 (libraries unix threads.posix effect4_eff effect4_clock effect4_bytes effect4_lcnf)
 (flags (:standard -w +a-4-9-40-41-42-44-45-70)))
